==Personality==
{{Quote|"What is it with you anyway, Albedo? You got what you wanted, you're a Galvan again! So go away and live out your little Galvan life somewhere, away from me!"<br>"And what? I am supposed to just forget the imprisonment? The humiliation? And the... [[Chili Fries|chili fries]]!?"|Ben and Albedo.<ref>''[[A Fistful of Brains]]''</ref>}}
Before he turned against Azmuth, Albedo was an eccentric genius who demonstrated quite an amount of respect toward Azmuth, and he showed concern for the safety of others. At the same time, however, he still displays an arrogant sense of superiority toward others in some aspects—mostly intelligence.<ref name="TH">''[[Trouble Helix]]''</ref>

In the present day, Albedo is arrogant, self-centered, ambitious, and bitter. He is also uncapable to accept [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]]'s right to being the wielder of the [[Omnitrix (Original)|Omnitrix]], thinking that he is just an unworthy human.<ref name="GCBC"/> Originally being a scientist, he speaks with a larger vocabulary, being more intellectual than Ben, though in a rather cold and condescending manner. He also refuses to take blame for his actions as shown when he blamed Ben for his form turning negative despite it being his fault that the pulse that turned his form negative was emitted. 

Because he had gained Ben's DNA, Albedo acquired Ben's cravings and habits, which he considers utterly repulsive: he has the same taste in food, scratches himself in "suspected" inappropriate places, and his left eye twitches whenever he lies. As a running gag of the series, he develops an insatiable craving for [[Chili Fries|chili fries]], even more than Ben himself, calling it a "human weakness." Originally, he had hated this habit, but develops a liking for them, though he denies this and blames it on his human DNA.

Albedo is suspicious and distrustful of others. During his brief team up with [[Vilgax (Classic)|Vilgax]], he had his suspicions of Vilgax betraying him from the very beginning, which is later proved correct after they had beaten Ben and taken his Omnitrix.

After absorbing Azmuth's intelligence, he briefly gained an enlightened personality, which led him to realize that destruction was pointless while creation was truly worthwhile. However, he soon reverted to his normal disposition after Azmuth's mind was extracted from him.

Despite his rude nature, he has shown to have a kind and nice attitude to his allies. The most notable instance is in the episode ''[[Double or Nothing]]'' where Albedo didn't blame [[Hugh]] for ruining his chance of becoming a complete Galvan again and instead blamed Ben, despite the fact that it was Hugh who lied to the team that Albedo was building a doomsday device, which is the reason the team went after Albedo (though the reason why he did it was because he didn't want Albedo to leave him).

==History==
===Background===
[[File:Trouble Helix (436).png|thumb|Albedo finishing the Helix|218x218px]]
Albedo was a brilliant young [[Galvan (Classic)|Galvan]] scientist, who served as [[Azmuth (Classic)|Azmuth]]'s assistant. In ''[[Trouble Helix]]'', he inadvertently had a hand in upgrading [[Malware]] into his current form when he was captured and forced to connect the new [[Helix]] with the old one. In the flashback, he was an ally of [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben Tennyson]] and was very loyal to Azmuth as he called him "First Thinker" and even fought for him when Malware approached.

At some point after, Albedo asked Azmuth for an [[Omnitrix (Original)|Omnitrix]] for himself, as he didn't trust "a mere [[Human (Classic)|human]]", though his request was denied, as Azmuth stated that there could be only one Omnitrix in the universe. Albedo then used his knowledge of the project to build a [[Omnitrix (Albedo's Replica)|copy]], and set it to match Ben's. However, when doing so, he didn't know that Ben's DNA would become the default, causing him to become permanently stuck as an exact clone of Ben.

These actions would ultimately lead Azmuth to fire him, though Albedo claims he quit.<ref name="FaFBM">''[[For a Few Brains More]]''</ref>

===Alien Force===
[[File:GCBC (513).png|thumb|left|Omnitrix Bio-Feedback|218x218px]]
Disgusted by what had happened to him, Albedo traveled to [[Earth (Classic)|Earth]] to get the [[Omnitrix (Original)|Omnitrix]] from [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] in ''[[Good Copy, Bad Copy]]'', planning on using it to restore his original form.

During his search for Ben, in at least three days, he savagely attacked at least three [[Forever Knights|Forever Knight]] castles and a [[DNAlien]] hive, for the purpose of interrogation to discover Ben's whereabouts, causing the Knights to believe Ben Tennyson was attacking them for no reason and attracting [[Gwen Tennyson (Classic)|Gwen]]'s and [[Kevin Levin (Classic)|Kevin]]'s attention. When Albedo and Ben eventually met during Albedo's siege at another castle, Albedo pretended to be the creator of the Omnitrix, accusing [[Azmuth (Classic)|Azmuth]] of being a liar, and asked Ben to hand it over. When Ben became suspicious and refused (after Kevin made him notice the twitch on his left eye each time he lied, which Ben has as well), Albedo transformed and attacked him in order to take his Omnitrix by force. After battling him twice, their Omnitrixes locked on with each other, almost causing feedback that could have destroyed the whole galaxy. During the process, Albedo's [[Human (Classic)|human]] form was damaged, resulting in him becoming a negative mirror of Ben. Azmuth then arrived and took off Albedo's Omnitrix's core, trapping him in his human form and sending him to an alien prison. Blaming Azmuth and Ben for his condition, Albedo swore to get revenge on them.

[[File:TFB1 (39).png|thumb|218x218px|Albedo with the [[Ultimatrix]]]]
In ''[[The Final Battle: Part 1|The Final]] [[The Final Battle: Part 2|Battle]]'', Albedo escaped from prison with the help of [[Vilgax (Classic)|Vilgax]], and stole the [[Ultimatrix (Original)|Ultimatrix]], an incomplete model of the Omnitrix, from Azmuth. Using pieces from his broken Omnitrix, he successfully completed the Ultimatrix and tried to use it in order to transform back to his Galvan form. However, the Ultimatrix was still linked to Ben's Omnitrix, leaving him trapped in his form. Vilgax then offered him an alliance, promising he would let him get Ben's Omnitrix. Though not really trusting him, Albedo accepted and helped him by kidnapping Gwen and Kevin. Despite the alliance being a success, Vilgax quickly double-crossed Albedo and made him his prisoner, using an army of thousands of [[Humungousaur (Classic)|Humungousaurs]] against him which defeated Albedo. After the Omnitrix was destroyed, Ben freed Albedo and forced him to hand over the Ultimatrix by triggering the self-destruct command. Though the ship then crashed into one of Earth's oceans, Albedo had escaped.

===Ultimate Alien===
When [[Kevin Levin (Classic)|Kevin]] and [[Gwen Tennyson (Classic)|Gwen]] put in [[Ultimatrix Security Keys|the Ultimatrix Security keys]] for [[Alien X (Classic)|Alien X]]'s transformation in ''[[The Forge of Creation]]'', [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] stated they did it so Albedo wouldn't get access to it if he took the Ultimatrix back or if there was a duplicate or otherwise, something similar in sync to it.

[[File:DoN (292).png|thumb|left|Albedo with his actors|218x218px]]
Albedo returned in ''[[Double or Nothing]]''; ever since [[Vilgax (Classic)|Vilgax]]'s ship blew up, Albedo was "broke and stranded" and had created his own live action show, 'Ben 10: Live', where Albedo played the role of Ben, and three of Ben's top most popular aliens, [[Swampfire]], [[Humungousaur (Classic)|Humungousaur]], and [[Big Chill (Classic)|Big Chill]], are played by three actors with fake Ultimatrix symbols: A [[Methanosian]] named [[Swamps]], a [[Vaxasaurian (Classic)|Vaxasaurian]] named [[Hugh]], and a [[Necrofriggian (Classic)|Necrofriggian]] named [[Fridge]].

After Albedo set a soundwave-bomb on the ground, Ben told Kevin and Gwen to 'deal with the bomb', while he went after Albedo. Albedo supposedly 'turned into' aliens, which were really just the real aliens replacing him before Ben saw the switch. When Ben battled all three of them, he told them that he knew they weren't Albedo. After talking to Albedo, telling him to never again do Ben 10: Live, Albedo stated that he wouldn't.

They were about to leave, but Hugh arrived and lied to the [[Alien Force|team]], saying Albedo was making a doomsday bomb that would make everyone on [[Earth (Classic)|Earth]] into a copy of Ben. They went to stop him at an old warehouse and saw Albedo wearing a large Omnitrix symbol on his chest, which Hugh said was going to protect him from the blast. Gwen questioned why Albedo would wear it if he already looked like Ben, but Ben cut her off and used [[NRG]] to blow a hole in the wall.

Albedo then yelled at the other aliens to keep them away. NRG defeated Swamps, and Gwen and Kevin defeated Fridge. Then, Hugh tried to defeat NRG, feigning he was on Albedo's side. [[Ultimate Spidermonkey]] went after Albedo, only to be reverted by the field surrounding Albedo. In their human forms, Albedo overpowered Ben and tried to worked on the "bomb", only for Ben to interfere again and cause the whole theater to suddenly blow up.

Albedo transformed back into his Galvan form, revealing that the machine wasn't a doomsday bomb, but rather a device to return him to a Galvan as well as making him able to alter his DNA at will, which he was able to afford to build with his performances. Restored to his Galvan form, he told Ben, who was expecting a fight with Albedo's new powers, there was no point in continuing their feud anymore, planning to get off Earth and never encounter Ben ever again. Unfortunately, he transformed back into Ben and found out, due to the Ultimatrix interrupting the device's alteration field, he would inevitably turn back into his human form.

[[File:DoN (446).png|thumb|Albedo's Galvan form ('''Ultimate Alien''')|218x218px]]
Hugh tried to take the blame and explained why he sabotaged Albedo's plan, but Albedo didn't blame him and instead furiously blamed Ben. Albedo then transformed into [[Rath (Classic)|Negative Rath]], and battled [[Echo Echo]]. When Negative Rath pinned Echo Echo down, Echo Echo went [[Ultimate Echo Echo]] and sent sound wave discs at Negative Rath. This caused Negative Rath to transform back to human and faint. Ben relinquished Albedo to the alien trio, but warned he wouldn't be happy when he woke up.

[[File:NotLN (494.1).png|thumb|left|218x218px|Albedo's nightmare]]
Albedo returned in ''[[Night of the Living Nightmare]]'', where he attempted to infect Ben with a [[Cassiopeian Dream Eater]], trapping him into a dream world where he kept being attacked by several of his enemies. Eventually, when Albedo entered the dream posing as Kevin and Gwen in an attempt to take the Ultimatrix, Ben figured out it was him from his friends stating he didn't deserve to bear the Ultimatrix and pursued him to Mr. Smoothy's.

As Ben started taking over the dream world and overpowered Negative Big Chill and NRG in human form, Albedo attempted to put back the Dream Eater, only to slip on a spilled smoothie and accidentally end up being the one infected. In the real world, it was revealed that Ben was never infected with the nightmare-inducing parasite. Albedo attempted to, but was dangerously unprepared for how messy Ben's room was, which resulted in him dropping the bug on his own face when he inadvertently slipped on a spilled smoothie, thus replaying the same thing that happened in Albedo's nightmare. While they called a Galvan doctor in order to properly remove the Dream Eater, Albedo was seen inside the dream world, being confronted by a group of the Ultimatrix aliens and fearfully begged them to not to hurt him as they came near. After getting it removed, he was imprisoned in the Plumbers HQ holding cells.

===Omniverse===
[[File:TUH (480).png|thumb|left|Albedo with the [[Ultimatrix (Stabilizer)|new Ultimatrix]]|218x218px]]
Albedo reappeared in the present day in ''[[The Ultimate Heist]]''. In it, he had been impersonating [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] for several days, after he and [[Khyber]] secretly switched his and Ben's places. Albedo did not use his alien transformations, due to the fact that the red eyes would give him away to Ben's allies. Even though his ruse was discovered and Ben escaped, Albedo managed to get what he [[Polymorphic Crystal|needed]] from [[Thirteen]]. The devices that he took would not only stabilize his transformations, allowing him to remain in them for as long as he wants, but allow him to once again access the [[Ultimate Forms]], including his own, [[Ultimate Albedo]].

In ''[[A Fistful of Brains]]'', Albedo tricked Ben into entering [[Khyber's Ship|Khyber's disguised ship]], capturing him and taking him to Khyber's private hunting area. Beforehand, Albedo had left toenail clippings and hair on several planets, in order to fool anyone who tried tracking Ben by his DNA.

[[File:Ultimate Albedo talking(2).png|thumb|Albedo in his Ultimate form|218x218px]]
Ben managed to escape Khyber and confronted Albedo. When Ben pointed out that Albedo had what he wanted, which was the power to return to his true [[Galvan (Classic)|Galvan]] form, Albedo informed him that he wanted revenge for his humiliation and imprisonment. Ben managed to overcome Ultimate Albedo, only for Ultimate Albedo to declare that Ben hadn't really won. Khyber then revealed that he had captured [[Azmuth (Classic)|Azmuth]].

In ''[[For a Few Brains More]]'', Ultimate Albedo intended to use the device he imprisoned Azmuth in, a [[Cerebral Vortex]], to drain Azmuth's intellect, and add it to his brainpower. Despite managing to drain Azmuth's intelligence into an orb form, Ben and company managed to free Azmuth and his intellect; however, after a lengthy battle, which culminated on [[Earth (Classic)|Earth]], Ultimate Albedo managed to escape to [[Billions Tower]], and used its lab to construct another Cerebral Vortex and added Azmuth's intellect to his own, easily subduing them. However, the combined brainpower led to Ultimate Albedo having an epiphany, realizing that destroying them was worthless, as they would still exist somewhere in the omniverse. This distraction allowed Ben to reverse the procedure, taking away Ultimate Albedo's stolen brainpower.

[[File:FaFBM (714).png|thumb|left|Negative Ultimate Spidermonkey defeated by Atomix|218x218px]]
Angered, Ultimate Albedo transformed into Negative [[Ultimate Humungousaur]] and began attacking Ben as [[Bloxx]], and pummeling him until he transformed back into normal and Azmuth hit the dial, transforming Ben into a new alien, [[Atomix]], who was easily able to beat Negative Ultimate Humungousaur and Negative [[Ultimate Spidermonkey]]. After having his intellect restored, Azmuth punished Albedo by reconfiguring his Ultimatrix to not only keep him as a clone of Ben, but as a clone of the 11-year-old Ben Tennyson. Mortified at this, Albedo cried.

[[File:ATTWN (297).png|thumb|Albedo with the evil Bens|218x218px]]
Albedo returned in ''[[And Then There Were None]]'', in which he and several other evil Bens joined forces with [[Vilgax (Classic)|Vilgax]] and [[Eon]] to wipe out every good Ben from the multiverse. However, he, along with the other evil Bens, was double-crossed by Vilgax and were erased from spacetime by a [[Chronosapien Time Bomb]].

In ''[[And Then There Was Ben]]'', he was brought back into existence by [[Ben Tennyson (No Watch Timeline)|No Watch Ben]]. Later, he chased an Omnitrixless [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben Tennyson]] as [[Ultimate Echo Echo|Negative Ultimate Echo Echo]] along with [[Mad Ben|Mad Ben]] and [[Bad Ben]]'s [[Buzzshock (Classic)|Buzzshock]]. At the end of the episode, he was sent back to the [[Prime Timeline]] by [[Clockwork]].

In ''[[Malgax Attacks]]'', Albedo and Vilgax infiltrated the [[Galvan Historical Museum]] to steal Malware's remains. While Vilgax fought Ben, Albedo attempted to obtain the secrets of Azmuth only to be stopped by [[Luhley]], [[Blukic]], [[Driba]], and Azmuth himself. He used [[Ultimate Rath]] to finish them all off until Azmuth disabled the Ultimatrix. Albedo was then sentenced to clean-up for the next "30 Galvan solar cycles", in which he demanded sunblock.

