==Weaknesses==
In almost all of his appearances, Albedo's own arrogance is often the source of his downfall and he always underestimates the intelligence and skill of those that oppose him, specifically Azmuth and Ben. His obsession and desire to get revenge on them can also lead him into getting into situations that end in his defeat and make him overlook the potential of others, such as when he all but completely ignored [[Blukic]] and [[Driba]] (due to their bumbling antics) while they successfully restored Azmuth after he had been destroyed by Albedo.

He has developed an uncontrollable craving for [[Chili Fries]]. This at times gets the better of him, such as side tracking him during or in-between his plans to pick some up. Another case is that he also has a hard time controlling himself eating them when he hasn't eaten any for a long period of time; when he is given some if this happens, he loses his self-control and eats them in a rather messy manner.

He needs his Ultimatrix (which is a stabilizer) in order to maintain his transformations and to turn into [[Ultimate Forms]]. Without it, he turns back into a human.

Despite his enhanced intelligence he doesn't judge people properly, seeing how he teamed up with [[Vilgax (Classic)|Vilgax]] thrice despite being betrayed by him on [[The Final Battle: Part 2|two]] [[And Then There Were None|occasions]].

